{\normalsize\bfseries\color{CoverCream} 關於本書}\qquad{\baskervillefont\itshape\normalsize\color{CoverGoldBright} About This Book}

\vspace{0.2cm}

\begin{minipage}{5in}
\setlength{\parskip}{0.15em}
\footnotesize\color{CoverCream}
$if(backcover)$
$backcover$
$else$
本書逐章研讀羅馬書全書十六章，並附索引與參考資料附錄，整合老弟兄一貫的查經方法論與以基督為中心的神學框架（本書並無對應之老弟兄羅馬書逐節查經筆記原始記錄，此為誠實說明，詳見附錄），alongside John MacArthur 逐節解經講道，以及 G. Campbell Morgan 的屬靈與結構分析。全信的軌跡，從全人類普世的罪、到因信稱義而不靠行為、到聖靈能力中的成聖生命、到神向以色列信實不變的揀選，直到一個被福音塑造的群體在世上當有的實際樣式——保羅寫給羅馬教會最系統的一封信，在這裡逐章展開。

{\baskervillefont\color{CoverCream} chapter-by-chapter study of all sixteen chapters of Romans, with index and references appendices, integrating the Elder's documented Bible-study methodology and Christ-centered theological framework (this book has no corresponding verse-by-verse Elder teaching notes on Romans itself --- an honest disclosure detailed in the appendix), alongside John MacArthur's verse-by-verse exposition and G. Campbell Morgan's spiritual and structural analysis. The letter's arc unfolds chapter by chapter: from the universal guilt of all humanity, through justification by faith apart from works, through the Spirit-empowered life of sanctification, through God's sovereign faithfulness to Israel, to the practical shape of a gospel-formed community in the world --- Paul's most systematic letter, traced here in full.}
$endif$
\end{minipage}

